## Pass/Fail Criteria

**PASS — All pipelines healthy:**
- All 16 tables have rows (count > 0)
- All vCMTS tables have data within the last 5 minutes
- All CM tables have data within the last 5 minutes
- SFID mapping returns valid us/ds service flow names for a known modem
- Latency, AQM drops, congestion marking, and sanctioned packet tables show data per modem/direction/sf_index
- Polling intervals are consistent (~15-30 seconds)
- vcmts-snapshot export generates valid CSV and Excel output

**FAIL — Pipeline issue detected:**
- Any table has 0 rows
- Any vCMTS table has stale data (last entry > 5 minutes old)
- Any CM table has stale data (last entry > 24 hours old — known issue, pipeline may have stopped)
- SFID mapping returns no results for a registered modem
- Latency or AQM tables return empty results for a modem that should have data
- Polling intervals show large gaps (> 2 minutes between samples)

## Known Issues
- **CM metrics pipeline stoppage**: The CM metrics tables (flow_stats, histogram_stats, congestion_stats, agg_flow_stats, vcmts_sfid_info) have previously stopped collecting data. If Step 4 shows stale CM data, escalate to investigate the collection pipeline.
- **qos_service_flow_packets/octets are NOT data-plane**: These counters only show management traffic (~28KB during a 421Mbps test). Do not use for throughput validation — use ByteBlower or iPerf3 results instead.
- **MAC format**: The database stores MACs in colon-separated lowercase (e.g. 0c:b9:37:64:3a:b0). The modem_metrics.py tool auto-converts from Cisco notation (0cb9.3764.3ab0) but raw SQL queries require colon format.
- **Polling interval**: vCMTS metrics poll every ~15 seconds. When aligning with test start/end times, widen the query window by ±30 seconds to capture bracketing samples.

## Notes
- Replace `<cm_mac>` with the actual cable modem MAC address (any format — the tool auto-converts)
- Replace `<cm_mac_colon_format>` with colon-separated lowercase MAC for raw SQL queries
- Replace `<start_time>` and `<end_time>` with actual timestamps in ISO format (e.g. "2026-04-08 17:57:00")
- The database is at 172.30.80.33:5433, dbname=modem_metrics, user=postgres